## Feature

Send a request to an actor and obtain its first reply as a value, bounded by a deadline, without the caller being an
actor.

## How Pekko solves it

Module: `actor` (classic) and `actor-typed`. Every ask creates its own `PromiseActorRef`; the reply address is the
correlation key. Classic and typed share this mechanism. Paths are under `upstream/pekko/`; `AS` is
`actor/src/main/scala/org/apache/pekko/pattern/AskSupport.scala` and `TA` is
`actor-typed/src/main/scala/org/apache/pekko/actor/typed/scaladsl/AskPattern.scala`.

**[Pekko]**

- Identity and correlation: one `Promise` and one `PromiseActorRef` per ask (`AS:711-744`). There is no correlation id;
  concurrent asks have distinct refs.
- Temporary ref: path `<prefix>$<base64 counter>` under `/temp`, registered lazily when `path` is first read
  (`AS:527-541, 592-612`; `ActorRefProvider.scala:428-441, 603-611`). A local ask whose ref is never inspected is never
  registered (`AS:667`).
- First reply wins: `tryComplete`; when it returns false the message goes to dead letters (`AS:614-629`).
  `PromiseRefSpec.scala:54-64` pins "the second message is a dead letter".
- Late reply after completion or stop: `DeadLetter(message, sender, this)` (`AS:614-629`); typed:
  `typed/AskSpec.scala:132, 164`.
- Timeout: `scheduleOnce`, then `tryComplete(Failure(onTimeout))` (`AS:725-738`). The reply and the timeout race through
  `tryComplete`. Classic fails with `AskTimeoutException`; typed fails with `java.util.concurrent.TimeoutException`
  (`TA:141`).
- Cleanup on every outcome: `result.future.onComplete { _ => a.stop(); f.cancel() }` (`AS:739-742`).
- Target already terminated: an immediate failure, and the message is still sent so it lands in dead letters
  (`AS:372-376`; `TA:146-163`; `AskSpec.scala:41, 50`; typed `AskSpec.scala:71, 109`). It is a point-in-time
  `isTerminated` check. **No watch is placed on the target during the wait**: typed `AskPattern` has no
  `RecipientTerminated`. A target that stops after the send is therefore not detected early by the ask itself.
- Non-positive timeout: `IllegalArgumentException` (`AS:377-378`; `AskSpec.scala:72, 83`).
- Error replies: classic `Status.Failure` fails the future (`AS:622`); typed `askWithStatus` and `StatusReply` separate
  mechanism errors from business errors (`StatusReply.scala:173-181`; typed `AskSpec.scala:267-281`).
- Per-actor ask: `ActorContext.ask` is `AskPattern.ask` plus `pipeToSelf` (`ActorContextImpl.scala:228-232`).

**[Unverified]**

- The remote reply path and ask across `ActorSystem`s (only `RemoteContextAskSpec.scala:76` was found, and it was not
  read in detail).
- `VirtualPathContainer` edge cases for a reply after unregistration.
- Ask on an `ActorSelection` with a terminated target (no `isTerminated` branch exists, `AS:455-468`).
- That Pekko never cancels a request already sent: this comes from the absence of any cancel mechanism in `AS`, not from a
  test.
- That a target stopping during the wait leaves the ask pending until timeout: this comes from reading `AS` and `TA`; no
  test pins it.

